  "body": "  A functor between our set-encoded categories is an equivalence if and only if it is fully faithful and essentially surjective.    First suppose has a quasi-inverse with comparisons . Essential surjectivity follows from . If , apply and conjugate by the components of to obtain ; hence is faithful. The same argument with shows that is faithful. Given , set . Naturality of at this arrow gives . Since is faithful, . Thus is full. This argument uses naturality rather than assuming unmentioned compatibility between the two comparisons.  Conversely, suppose is fully faithful and essentially surjective. For every , choose an object and an isomorphism . These choices are indexed by the set , and the possible pairs form sets, so the axiom of choice supplies them. No choice indexed by a proper class is being made.  For an arrow , define to be the unique lift under full faithfulness of The image of is an identity, so faithfulness gives . The image of equals the product of the images of and , by cancellation of the middle factors; faithfulness gives . Hence is a functor. Its defining equation makes natural.  For each , let be the unique lift of . It is invertible by . For , the definition of yields Faithfulness makes natural. Both comparisons have invertible components, so they are natural isomorphisms by . This proves the equivalence.   "
