  "body": "  Both iterated limits above are limits of over . There is a unique isomorphism preserving all maps to . Dually, whenever both iterated colimits exist, they are canonically isomorphic as colimits of the product-indexed diagram.    A map from into is a family of maps from into the inner limits, compatible in . Expanding each inner universal property gives maps compatible in . Compatibility in is equivalent to the component equations in every , since maps to each inner limit are determined by its projections. Thus the resulting families are precisely those compatible separately in both variables.  Such a family is a cone over . Indeed, an arrow factors as the arrow changing and the arrow changing . Separate compatibility gives compatibility with their composite; the converse follows by taking one arrow to be an identity. The same expansion for describes exactly the same cones. The bijections preserve every leg, so both objects are limiting cones of , and uniqueness of limits gives the asserted isomorphism. Duality proves the colimit assertion.   "
