  "number": "7.10",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  If every has a left Kan extension along , choose these extensions. They determine a functor left adjoint to . If all right extensions exist, their choices determine a functor right adjoint to . Thus, when both exist,    For , define by the unique equation Identity and composition follow from this uniqueness. The defining bijection for left extensions is natural in ; the displayed equation makes it natural in as well, proving . The right-hand construction is dual. Equivalently, these are the universal-arrow criterion applied in the two functor categories. Their object sets are sets, so choosing the extensions uses ordinary choice.   "
