  "body": " Free cocompletion Restricted nerve   Let , with  -cocomplete. Define There is an adjunction , and a canonical natural isomorphism . Moreover, restriction along gives an equivalence where the subscript denotes the full subcategory of functors preserving -small colimits. Every such functor is a left adjoint.    A map is a compatible family . Sending to identifies it with a map for each . The compatibility equation from says exactly that these maps form a natural transformation. Thus naturally in both variables. Universal maps make functorial; ordinary choice supplies one colimit for each presheaf, if no choices have been fixed. Since the collection of presheaves is an ordinary set, this uses the choice convention of . The formula gives the adjunction and therefore preservation of small colimits.  Setting and applying Yoneda identifies the right side with , naturally in . Uniqueness of representing objects gives . Explicitly, the cocone consists of for ; the category of these pairs has terminal object .  Now let preserve small colimits. Applying it to the density presentation gives, naturally in , This recovers every colimit-preserving functor from its restriction; essential surjectivity of restriction follows from . A natural transformation induces by applying to every colimit summand. Conversely, a transformation between two colimit-preserving functors is determined by its components on representables: its component at must commute with every map , and the colimit cocone is jointly epic. The induced transformation has exactly that property, proving fullness as well as faithfulness. Finally gives its right adjoint .   "
