  "body": " Monadicity  Monadic functor   The adjunction is monadic if its comparison is an equivalence. A functor is monadic if it has a left adjoint whose comparison is an equivalence. Requiring the comparison to be an isomorphism of categories is a stronger, presentation-dependent condition, sometimes called strict monadicity.   "
