  "number": "9.26",
  "title": "",
  "body": " Cofree coalgebra   The functor , , is right adjoint to . Its bijection and inverse are The forgetful functor creates all existing small colimits of underlying diagrams. An adjunction , with , induces the comonad with the adjunction counit, and the comparison functor sends to .    Apply the free-algebra adjunction and creation-of-limits theorem to the monad on , then reverse arrows. The transpose formulas become exactly those displayed. Applying the adjunction-monad construction to gives the indicated comultiplication and comparison after reversing arrows. Thus no preservation of colimits by is needed for the creation assertion.   "
