  "number": "9.27",
  "title": "Beck’s comonadicity theorem.",
  "body": " Beck's comonadicity theorem  Comonadic functor   For as above, the comparison is an equivalence if and only if is conservative and every -split parallel pair has an equalizer in which preserves. In this case is called comonadic.    This is the Beck theorem already proved, applied to the right adjoint and then translated by the displayed opposite-category identifications. Conservativity is self-dual, while split coequalizers become the stated split equalizers.   "
