  "type": "Example",
  "number": "9.28",
  "title": "A coalgebra can record a map to a fixed set.",
  "body": " A coalgebra can record a map to a fixed set  Fix . On sets let , let , and let . These formulas satisfy the comonad laws by evaluation on pairs. A coalgebra structure on must be for a function , by the counit equation. Its coassociativity equation then holds automatically. A function is a coalgebra map exactly when . Thus is isomorphic to the slice .  The forgetful functor is the domain functor ; its cofree right adjoint sends to the projection . All formulas include , when the coalgebra category has only the empty set. Coalgebras for a comonad need not be algebraic coalgebras over a field, just as algebras for a monad need not be rings or vector spaces. The specified endofunctor and structure maps determine the meaning.  "
