  "number": "12.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  For filtered presentations and , there is a natural bijection The limit and colimit on the right are formed in . The opposite on the source index records contravariance of Hom in its first argument.    Fullness, the universal property of the source colimit, Yoneda, and pointwise evaluation give, respectively, Each bijection is induced by the specified cocones and is natural in the objects. No exchange of a finite limit with a filtered colimit occurs in this proof.   "
