  "body": " Exponentials and cartesian closure  Exponential object Cartesian closed category Currying   For objects , an exponential of by consists of an object and an evaluation arrow such that, for every , the function is bijective. The inverse sends to its transpose, or curried arrow, denoted . A category is cartesian closed if it has finite products, including a terminal object, and an exponential for every pair .   "
