  "number": "14.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  In a cartesian closed category, chosen exponentials have the following properties.   Evaluation and transposition satisfy  For and , there is a unique arrow satisfying These arrows define a functor , .  For , , and as above, transposition satisfies In particular, for each fixed , is left adjoint to .     The first equations say that the defining functions are inverse. Define by transposing the right side of its evaluation equation. Evaluating an identity or a composite of these arrows gives the corresponding identity or composite precomposition and postcomposition on product maps. Uniqueness of transposes proves the functor laws. Likewise, evaluation of gives , proving the displayed naturality formula. Its cases with are exactly the two naturality conditions for the asserted adjunction.   "
