  "number": "14.4",
  "title": "Groups are not cartesian closed.",
  "body": " Groups are not cartesian closed  The trivial group is both initial and terminal in . If were an exponential, then would be a singleton. Take : its identity and zero homomorphism are distinct. Thus does not exist as a cartesian exponential in the group category, despite the existence of finite products there.  "
