  "body": "  For  -small and , there is an equivalence In particular, is locally cartesian closed.    For , assign to the fiber An arrow in the element category satisfies . Restriction therefore gives a map from the fiber over to the fiber over , by naturality of . This defines a presheaf on ; maps over restrict to maps of these fibers.  Conversely, given a presheaf on , set For , send to , where is the associated element-category arrow. The functor laws for give the presheaf laws for , and projection onto gives . Maps of presheaves induce maps of these sums. Passing from a family to its sum and back to its fibers gives the natural comparison isomorphisms, proving the equivalence.  The category is -small by the element-category size bound. Its presheaf category is therefore cartesian closed by . Equivalences preserve the representing properties of products and exponentials, so the slice on the left is cartesian closed. Finally, finite limits of presheaves exist pointwise, which verifies our finite-limit convention for local closure.   "
