  "number": "15.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "   Every split epimorphism is regular, every regular epimorphism is strong, and every strong epimorphism is epic.  A strong epimorphism that is monic is an isomorphism. More generally, if a strong epimorphism factors through a monomorphism, that monomorphism is invertible.  If a regular epimorphism has a kernel pair, it is the coequalizer of that kernel pair.     If has section , it coequalizes . A map with factors as , uniquely because is epic. Hence is their coequalizer.  Suppose coequalizes and with monic. Then , so . There is a unique with . The equation and epicity of a coequalizer give . Thus .  If with monic and strong, apply lifting to top map and bottom identity. It gives with . Monicity also gives , so is invertible. Taking proves the special case.  Finally write for the kernel pair of . Any original pair coequalized by factors through this pair by pullback. Therefore a map coequalizing the kernel pair coequalizes the original pair and factors uniquely through , as required.   "
