  "id": "cat-c15-prop-kernel-pair",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "cat-images-regular.html#cat-c15-prop-kernel-pair",
  "type": "Proposition",
  "number": "15.5",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  A kernel pair defines an internal equivalence relation. For generalized elements , its relation is exactly . Moreover, is monic if and only if its kernel pair is the diagonal relation, equivalently if the diagonal is invertible.    The pullback identifies maps with pairs having equal composites under . The associated map to is monic because its two projections determine each map into the pullback. Equality after is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, and the preceding test constructs the three internal maps. Its relation is equality for every precisely when is monic. In that case the diagonal and either projection are inverse; the converse follows by testing any pair with equal images.   "
