  "type": "Proposition",
  "number": "16.4",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  A cleavage determines a functor for every . On a vertical , its arrow is characterized by Every over factors uniquely as It is cartesian if and only if is an isomorphism.    Apply the property of to over . The resulting vertical arrow defines . Uniqueness, applied to identities and successive vertical arrows, gives the functor laws. The same property with gives its unique factorization. If is invertible, the composite is cartesian. If is cartesian, cancellation makes cartesian; being vertical, it is then invertible.   "
